WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.584
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will make alerts reach the

00:00:05.584 --> 00:00:11.169
intended audience. Repeated messages create noise, while incomplete contacts and device preferences can

00:00:11.169 --> 00:00:16.753
leave intended recipients unreachable. We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and

00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:19.760
a practical way to check the result.

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:25.711
An administrator creates notification rules for new calls, builds an Officers distribution list

00:00:25.711 --> 00:00:31.063
and runs a communication test before going live. A dispatch only helps if

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:36.414
it reaches people. This is where you confirm members can actually be contacted.

00:00:36.414 --> 00:00:41.765
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios,

00:00:41.765 --> 00:00:43.000
not default settings.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.440
Notification rules. Rules that alert chosen people when calls, statuses or other events

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.281
happen. Create notification rules for the events officers and administrators need to know

00:00:55.281 --> 00:00:55.730
about.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:03.292
Distribution lists. Reusable recipient lists, including email lists. Create lists for groups you

00:01:03.292 --> 00:01:05.970
message often, such as Officers.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:12.284
Communication Tests. Test messages that show whether members can be reached. Run a

00:01:12.284 --> 00:01:16.240
communication test before going live and after major changes.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:22.003
Chat. Team chat for members. Create channels for your teams once chat is

00:01:22.003 --> 00:01:22.400
enabled.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:28.346
Inbox. Messages sent to you. Make sure members have added a mobile number

00:01:28.346 --> 00:01:33.692
or email address and installed the Responder app. Availability also depends on Messaging.

00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:36.160
Check access in the target department.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.125
Sent Messages. Messages you have sent. Make sure members have added a mobile

00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:47.491
number or email address and installed the Responder app. Availability also depends on

00:01:47.491 --> 00:01:50.380
Messaging. Check access in the target department.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:56.283
New Message. Send a message, poll or callback request to members. Make sure

00:01:56.283 --> 00:02:01.585
members have added a mobile number or email address and installed the Responder

00:02:01.585 --> 00:02:06.480
app. Availability also depends on Messaging. Check access in the target department.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:11.936
Chatbot and Assistant integration settings. Connect the Resgrid Assistant to chat platforms and

00:02:11.936 --> 00:02:16.792
choose what it may do. Make sure members have added a mobile number

00:02:16.792 --> 00:02:19.780
or email address and installed the Responder app.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:26.077
Account linking associates a member with a configured external assistant platform. Confirm a

00:02:26.077 --> 00:02:31.774
platform is configured, generate a short-lived linking code, and complete linking in the

00:02:31.774 --> 00:02:37.470
intended platform. Review the linked identity and a controlled permitted action. Keep the

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:43.167
temporary code out of the recording. Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.920
recording the live workflow.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:51.715
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Confirm member contacts

00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:57.909
and notification preferences. Step 2. Create an Officers distribution list and a focused

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:04.104
notification rule. Step 3. Run an explicit communication test and review the recorded

00:03:04.104 --> 00:03:04.580
outcomes.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:10.993
Now verify the result. Ask test recipients to confirm the actual channel and

00:03:10.993 --> 00:03:16.806
time received. Review missing or failed results and the intended audience. A common

00:03:16.806 --> 00:03:22.619
problem to watch for: A provider handoff is not confirmed delivery. Staffing suppression,

00:03:22.619 --> 00:03:27.090
recipient selection, and contact eligibility each deserve a separate check.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:33.386
Your practice task is simple. Send only to the demo audience. Record recipients,

00:03:33.386 --> 00:03:39.081
observed receipts, failures, and follow-up actions; compare with the expected audience. Record the

00:03:39.081 --> 00:03:44.777
result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the

00:03:44.777 --> 00:03:48.720
linked feature scripts for the detailed screen recording plan.

